    distribute, sublicense, and/or sell copies of the Software, and to
    permit persons to whom the Software is furnished to do so, subject to
    the following conditions:

    The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included
    in all copies or substantial portions of the Software.

    THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS
    OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF
    MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT.
    IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY
    CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT,
    TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE
    SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.


2. Code derived from the Half-Life SDK and from Paranoia
--------------------------------------------------------

Much of src/ (the game DLLs, the shared code and the SDK headers) descends
from the Half-Life 1 SDK, Copyright (c) Valve Corp. That code is subject to
the Half-Life 1 SDK License, whose full text is in
LICENSES/Half-Life-1-SDK.txt: it may be copied, modified and distributed in
source and object code form, but only for free.

Code that descends from Paranoia (the client.dll renderer, and the Paranoia
and Spirit of Half-Life code in both game DLLs) keeps Paranoia's terms:
GPL-2.0 for Paranoia's own code and the Half-Life 1 SDK License for Valve's
files (see docs/refs.md).


3. Code and data reconstructed from the Cry of Fear binaries
------------------------------------------------------------

The rest of src/ (apart from the code of part 4 and the third-party code
named there), and the names and addresses of retail functions and data
in tools/symbols/ and docs/*.csv, reproduce code and facts of the retail
Cry of Fear binaries. Their copyright belongs to their original authors:
Team Psykskallar (Cry of Fear), Valve Corporation (the GoldSrc engine, VGUI2
and the engine launcher) and the authors of the third-party code compiled
into the game. This license grants no rights over that code. It is
published for research, preservation and interoperability with a legally
owned copy of the game.


4. Code written for ReCoF
-------------------------

The code ReCoF adds to the game is under the MIT License of part 1,
Copyright (c) 2026 caixax:

  - the files written for ReCoF: src/cl_dll/rc_*, src/dlls/rc_*,
    src/gameui/Rc*, and any other file whose header says it was written
    for ReCoF;
  - every change ReCoF made to the other files of src/ after it was forked
    from DeCoF. The git history shows each one, and most are marked with a
    "ReCoF" comment.

Such a change may be reused on its own under the MIT License. A file that
descends from the Half-Life SDK or Paranoia keeps the terms of part 2 as a
whole, with ReCoF's changes in it, and code reconstructed from the retail
binaries stays under part 3 however much of it ReCoF changed.

src/external/ holds third-party code under the licenses that come with it:
the discord-rpc fork of YaLTeR (Discord's discord-rpc, MIT) and RapidJSON
(Tencent and Milo Yip, MIT), both submodules, and the Khronos OpenGL headers
in GL/ and KHR/ (The Khronos Group, MIT).


ReCoF and DeCoF are not affiliated with or endorsed by Team Psykskallar or
Valve. No game assets or retail binaries are part of this repository.
